WEBVTT

00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:06.650
<b>GUNDAM
VICTORY
MOBILE SUIT</b>

00:00:06.650 --> 00:00:12.610
The furious rain, Makes my heart shake
hageshii ame ga, kokoro wo yuruwaseru

00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:15.820
Like it did on that day
Ano hi no youni

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:22.910
But I just ran through, In my dream I had till yesterday
Tada hashirinuketa, kinou made no MY DREAM

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:26.710
...I still believe
...shinjiteiru no sa

00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:34.470
I'm willing to fight, An endless defense
Owari no nai, defense demo ii yo

00:00:35.090 --> 00:00:42.350
As long as you, Keep on gazing at me
Kimi ga boku wo, mitsumetsuzukete kureru nara

00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:45.270
STAND UP TO THE VICTORY!

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:50.980
Turn to face all the mornings ahead, And someday
Ikutsumono asa wo mukae, Itsuka kitto

00:00:52.070 --> 00:00:53.860
Try to seize them
tsukande miseru

00:00:53.990 --> 00:00:56.450
STAND UP TO THE VICTORY!

00:00:56.780 --> 00:01:02.120
Even if nothing, Lies on the other side
Sono mukougawa ni, nanimonakutemo

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:06.040
It doesn't matter to me
kamawanai kara

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:14.050
...Just as long as I can embrace, Your gentle, irreplaceable smile!
Kakegae no nai, kimi no yasashii egao daite

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:26.960
A funeral.

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:30.930
It made Üso understand the reality of a battlefield.

00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:34.300
Even so, Shrike Team and Üso...

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:39.330
...fought to protect the mass driver rail which carries ships into space.

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:42.630
Amidst it, Kite Bush died...

00:01:42.900 --> 00:01:46.430
...protecting the shuttle which carried Katejina aboard.

00:01:47.560 --> 00:01:49.500
Üso wept.

00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:51.860
They killed Miss Kite!

00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:55.260
SPACE DUST

00:01:55.260 --> 00:01:56.930
"Space Dust".
SPACE DUST

00:01:56.930 --> 00:01:57.530
SPACE DUST

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:15.700
This shuttle has empty seats, and I even have tickets. Here!

00:02:15.960 --> 00:02:19.130
Üso, you should go into space and find your parents.

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:20.160
Shahkti...

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:24.000
I'll wait for your mother to come back in Kasarelia.

00:02:25.060 --> 00:02:27.060
You're going back to Kasarelia from here?

00:02:27.100 --> 00:02:30.360
Odelo and the others said they wanted to live there too, right?

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:31.930
Yes, but...

00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:34.260
Flight 671 is on schedule.

00:02:34.860 --> 00:02:37.960
Winds out of the northeast at 3 m/sec, visibility, good.

00:02:40.100 --> 00:02:41.930
Flanders, stop.

00:02:43.230 --> 00:02:44.260
Haro!

00:02:54.130 --> 00:02:55.100
Clear.

00:02:55.330 --> 00:02:56.300
Okay.

00:02:56.330 --> 00:03:00.300
If we use the reserve batteries, the pilots shouldn't notice.

00:03:00.330 --> 00:03:02.000
Countdown to ignition.

00:03:02.130 --> 00:03:03.230
Starting.

00:03:03.260 --> 00:03:05.060
All right, magnetic flux reading?

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:07.960
Nominal. Linear motor, start!

00:03:13.900 --> 00:03:17.430
Shahkti! Odelo and Warren are gone!

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:19.360
Shahkti, do you know where they are?!

00:03:19.630 --> 00:03:22.000
I can't find them anywhere!

00:03:22.260 --> 00:03:23.600
They wouldn't...

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:36.100
Nothing's stopping this shuttle, now.

00:03:36.130 --> 00:03:37.000
Right.

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:43.000
I'm going to space to meet up with Jinn Jahannam, so I can't give you any help.

00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:44.400
Understood.

00:03:44.660 --> 00:03:48.160
I'll be looking for my parents, so I can't help you either, Miss Marbet.

00:03:48.630 --> 00:03:49.660
Fine.

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:52.930
You heard that from below, right?

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:54.330
Y-Yeah...

00:03:54.760 --> 00:03:57.200
Kid, can you open the floor hatch?

00:03:57.300 --> 00:03:58.200
Sure.

00:04:02.060 --> 00:04:03.130
Stowaways?

00:04:03.160 --> 00:04:04.160
Excuse us!

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:05.300
Odelo!

00:04:05.560 --> 00:04:06.630
Sorry.

00:04:06.660 --> 00:04:07.900
Warren, too?

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:09.760
What's the meaning of this?!

00:04:09.800 --> 00:04:11.160
Suzy was crying!

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:13.430
What, we should have brought a little kid, too?!

00:04:13.460 --> 00:04:18.300
Miss Marbet, we'd better take pictures of us threatening the corporation pilot,

00:04:18.330 --> 00:04:19.930
or it might be bad later.

00:04:19.960 --> 00:04:21.060
A threat photo?

00:04:21.100 --> 00:04:24.830
Right. Okay, point your gun at Captain Genis.

00:04:26.460 --> 00:04:27.960
Before you do, put this on!

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:28.860
What's...

00:04:28.900 --> 00:04:30.000
Pantyhose.

00:04:30.460 --> 00:04:33.630
Here... Like this. There we go.

00:04:35.830 --> 00:04:37.160
For crying out loud...

00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:42.100
Now I'll take some.

00:04:54.930 --> 00:04:56.160
Sis?

00:04:56.930 --> 00:04:59.760
Let's go into space, too, then.

00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:04.160
Really? You really think we can?

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:05.330
We can.

00:05:05.900 --> 00:05:10.130
Because that rail leads to where we need to go.

00:05:23.860 --> 00:05:26.830
Kasarelia must be further up.

00:05:28.230 --> 00:05:31.300
This is the best view ever! Warren!

00:05:31.560 --> 00:05:33.200
Get the Earth in the background!

00:05:33.230 --> 00:05:34.160
Yeah yeah!

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:35.930
Come on, you...

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:37.730
Zero gravity. Be careful.

00:05:37.760 --> 00:05:38.730
How about now?

00:05:38.760 --> 00:05:40.230
You're upside down!

00:05:40.560 --> 00:05:42.800
Take it, then I'll get you, Warren.

00:05:42.830 --> 00:05:44.000
Okay!

00:05:57.300 --> 00:06:00.600
Thank you, Lieutenant. We've made orbit, on schedule.

00:06:01.100 --> 00:06:03.360
No, I was adding extra weight.

00:06:03.400 --> 00:06:05.200
It probably made things harder for you, Captain.

00:06:05.430 --> 00:06:07.560
Come into the cabin and rest.

00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:08.960
Thanks, I will.

00:06:18.630 --> 00:06:23.230
We've circled the Earth a few extra orbits, but it looks like we're in our target airspace now.

00:06:23.260 --> 00:06:24.860
Again, thanks to you, Lieutenant.

00:06:24.900 --> 00:06:26.000
Don't be sarcastic.

00:06:26.030 --> 00:06:27.230
I'm not.

00:06:28.930 --> 00:06:30.200
Are you used to space, yet?

00:06:30.230 --> 00:06:31.060
Yes.

00:06:31.130 --> 00:06:33.400
Why don't I get us something to drink?

00:06:33.430 --> 00:06:34.260
Sure.

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:38.660
Okay, just use your legs to kick lightly away from the ceiling.

00:06:38.700 --> 00:06:39.900
R-Right...

00:06:40.760 --> 00:06:41.860
There you go.

00:06:42.030 --> 00:06:43.160
Sorry.

00:06:44.030 --> 00:06:45.160
You'll get used to it.

00:06:45.200 --> 00:06:46.600
Ltjg. Cronicle.

00:06:46.630 --> 00:06:47.660
Yes?

00:06:47.960 --> 00:06:51.230
It looks like the Keilas Guilie Fleet is starting another battle.

00:06:52.700 --> 00:06:56.530
The only other name I'm hearing mentioned is the Bagley Team.

00:06:56.700 --> 00:06:59.160
Does the Federation have a unit by that name?

00:06:59.200 --> 00:07:01.360
No, not that I've heard of.

00:07:01.760 --> 00:07:04.100
It's probably part of the League Militaire.

00:07:04.160 --> 00:07:06.230
Can you go have a look?

00:07:06.400 --> 00:07:07.660
Yes, ma'am.

00:07:07.930 --> 00:07:08.900
Lieutenant?

00:07:25.030 --> 00:07:27.400
We've come to space, but there's still war.

00:07:45.460 --> 00:07:47.460
Only one ship left, already?

00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:49.900
They'd really go against the Keilas Guilie Fleet,

00:07:49.930 --> 00:07:52.530
commanded by Captain Tassilo Wago?

00:07:54.030 --> 00:07:56.160
I'll try firing a flare to offer them a chance to surrender.

00:08:03.200 --> 00:08:05.160
Signal flare, dead astern!

00:08:07.960 --> 00:08:09.960
This battle is meaningless!

00:08:15.700 --> 00:08:17.960
I'm advising the rebels to surrender!

00:08:25.360 --> 00:08:28.160
A signal for surrender?! Did our flagship go down?

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:30.260
There's no doubt about it! What do we do?

00:08:30.300 --> 00:08:32.130
We'll just have to surrender.

00:08:42.600 --> 00:08:45.360
One Federation battleship, captured.

00:08:52.760 --> 00:08:53.960
I don't believe this!

00:08:54.000 --> 00:08:55.730
This is the last thing we need right now!

00:08:55.760 --> 00:08:56.630
What was that?

00:08:56.660 --> 00:08:59.100
Garbage. Space debris.

00:08:59.130 --> 00:08:59.800
Garbage?

00:08:59.830 --> 00:09:00.730
Dammit!

00:09:00.760 --> 00:09:01.960
Can we change course?

00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:04.760
If we could, I wouldn't be worrying like this!

00:09:05.400 --> 00:09:07.830
Those lights aren't stars?

00:09:14.060 --> 00:09:15.230
What's wrong?

00:09:15.260 --> 00:09:18.030
It's a zone full of asteroids and colony wreckage!

00:09:18.700 --> 00:09:20.560
I'll break out normal suits for everyone!

00:09:20.660 --> 00:09:21.700
Please do!

00:09:21.730 --> 00:09:26.500
Marbet, as a pilot cadet, monitor the shuttle and maintain our course!

00:09:27.600 --> 00:09:28.860
Thanks.

00:09:28.900 --> 00:09:29.960
Will we be okay?

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:31.760
It happens a lot.

00:09:39.260 --> 00:09:40.430
He's started.

00:09:40.930 --> 00:09:41.760
Yeah.

00:09:55.830 --> 00:09:59.000
Captain, I'm reading a fairly large piece of debris approaching.

00:09:59.200 --> 00:10:00.160
How's the barrier?

00:10:01.130 --> 00:10:02.260
Unstable.

00:10:02.460 --> 00:10:04.400
We had an air leak.

00:10:05.130 --> 00:10:07.300
Shouldn't be too much of a problem.

00:10:08.730 --> 00:10:09.860
Can you tell which direction?

00:10:09.900 --> 00:10:11.200
10 o'clock!

00:10:11.230 --> 00:10:12.560
Fire number 10 apogee motor!

00:10:12.600 --> 00:10:13.460
Yes, sir.

00:10:13.960 --> 00:10:15.000
The barrier!

00:10:24.430 --> 00:10:26.300
Captain Genis. what happened?!

00:10:26.330 --> 00:10:27.630
Please respond!

00:10:27.800 --> 00:10:29.430
His lifeline's stretching out.

00:10:29.460 --> 00:10:31.830
Miss Marbet, isn't there any response?!

00:10:31.860 --> 00:10:33.160
He's unconscious.

00:10:33.900 --> 00:10:36.430
You've never done a spacewalk, have you?!

00:10:36.930 --> 00:10:40.460
You need to stay here and protect the shuttle, Miss Marbet!

00:10:40.500 --> 00:10:42.100
An Earthnoid can't handle this!

00:10:42.130 --> 00:10:43.430
I'm gonna try!

00:10:48.100 --> 00:10:50.060
You can hear the vibrations when our helmets touch!

00:10:50.100 --> 00:10:51.000
Right.

00:10:51.030 --> 00:10:52.930
Switch on the radio on your waist.

00:10:54.460 --> 00:10:57.400
Stick a balloon on the spot that was just hit.

00:10:57.560 --> 00:10:58.360
Balloon?

00:10:58.400 --> 00:10:59.330
Birdlime.

00:10:59.360 --> 00:11:02.000
It's used to make emergency repairs to hull breaches.

00:11:04.630 --> 00:11:05.800
It's the...

00:11:05.830 --> 00:11:07.200
...entire Earth.

00:11:30.560 --> 00:11:31.400
Don't panic!

00:11:31.430 --> 00:11:32.600
Use your air gun!

00:11:32.630 --> 00:11:34.060
It's on the belt at your waist!

00:11:35.030 --> 00:11:37.660
A-Air gun? This thing?

00:11:41.030 --> 00:11:42.900
Use the air gun gently!

00:11:43.130 --> 00:11:44.960
Easy for you to say!

00:11:45.330 --> 00:11:47.230
Why is the shuttle upside down now?

00:11:47.260 --> 00:11:49.330
You're the one who's upside down!

00:11:49.630 --> 00:11:51.360
Pull on the captain's rope.

00:11:51.400 --> 00:11:52.030
Right.

00:11:52.200 --> 00:11:54.960
Üso, do you see the switch for the rope winch?

00:11:55.100 --> 00:11:56.400
Um... Yeah.

00:11:56.700 --> 00:11:57.700
I'm winding it in.

00:11:57.730 --> 00:11:58.900
Take it slow.

00:12:01.830 --> 00:12:03.700
Won't he be pulled into the hull?

00:12:03.730 --> 00:12:06.330
He may bounce, but he should be okay.

00:12:08.530 --> 00:12:10.800
Careful! Don't rush.

00:12:32.100 --> 00:12:35.930
If you have something to say, I'll listen, Commander Fuala.

00:12:35.960 --> 00:12:39.960
The failure at Gibraltar was entirely my responsibility.

00:12:40.260 --> 00:12:42.830
I'll accept whatever ruling the court martial makes.

00:12:44.330 --> 00:12:46.430
There's no need to wait for a court martial's ruling.

00:12:46.460 --> 00:12:48.560
I am the court martial!

00:13:01.200 --> 00:13:03.130
Okay, Üso. Get back here, now!

00:13:03.160 --> 00:13:04.700
We'll treat him inside!

00:13:06.100 --> 00:13:07.100
Where's Warren?

00:13:07.130 --> 00:13:08.660
He went to seal the air leak.

00:13:09.030 --> 00:13:10.130
It's toward the nose?

00:13:10.160 --> 00:13:11.130
Yeah.

00:13:16.360 --> 00:13:17.400
You okay?

00:13:17.430 --> 00:13:18.730
I can handle it.

00:13:22.830 --> 00:13:25.430
Try pushing in the second unit from the right.

00:13:25.460 --> 00:13:26.460
This?

00:13:29.360 --> 00:13:31.460
No good! I'll evade.

00:13:36.900 --> 00:13:37.630
Ow!

00:13:37.660 --> 00:13:38.860
Captain? Ow!

00:13:40.200 --> 00:13:42.030
Marbet, what happened?

00:13:42.430 --> 00:13:45.060
We can't make it through the oncoming debris, Captain!

00:13:45.360 --> 00:13:47.560
Just nose us up two degrees!

00:13:47.800 --> 00:13:50.030
Victory's in the cargo bay, right?

00:13:50.560 --> 00:13:52.330
Marbet's mobile suit?

00:13:52.360 --> 00:13:53.060
Yes.

00:13:53.100 --> 00:13:54.930
I'll clear the debris with that.

00:13:54.960 --> 00:13:56.100
That's reckless!

00:13:56.400 --> 00:13:58.460
Mobile suits were originally made for construction-

00:13:58.500 --> 00:14:01.400
I'm saying you don't know how to use the Victory in space!

00:14:01.430 --> 00:14:04.800
Try it. You're the genius pilot, aren't you?

00:14:04.830 --> 00:14:05.530
But...

00:14:05.560 --> 00:14:09.730
The shuttle's already in bad condition because we couldn't service it properly.

00:14:10.160 --> 00:14:11.960
You know the reason, right?

00:14:13.500 --> 00:14:17.160
We didn't want to fight in Arti Gibraltar.

00:14:31.330 --> 00:14:35.460
If you use the Gundam's thrusters, you'll alter the shuttle's course.

00:14:42.330 --> 00:14:43.300
Nice!

00:14:44.700 --> 00:14:45.660
The rifle...

00:14:45.700 --> 00:14:46.660
Hurry!

00:14:46.700 --> 00:14:47.930
I know!

00:14:52.100 --> 00:14:54.800
Crap, incoming! Incoming! Just below the nose!

00:14:54.830 --> 00:14:57.130
Shut up! Lower your volume!

00:14:57.160 --> 00:14:58.600
I'm using the rifle.

00:15:09.630 --> 00:15:11.660
Look! Below us, 11 o'clock!

00:15:11.830 --> 00:15:13.500
A dead branch? Why is that...

00:15:13.530 --> 00:15:14.730
Ask the garbage!

00:15:20.030 --> 00:15:21.700
A building! A big one!

00:15:21.730 --> 00:15:22.930
A building?

00:15:26.160 --> 00:15:27.360
Increase the power!

00:15:27.400 --> 00:15:29.730
Too risky! I'll use the shield!

00:15:40.430 --> 00:15:42.660
Whew! Nice job, Üso!

00:15:42.700 --> 00:15:43.730
Look.

00:15:51.700 --> 00:15:53.700
Delicious ice cream, isn't it?

00:15:54.930 --> 00:15:55.930
Yes.

00:15:56.030 --> 00:15:57.230
As I'd expect.

00:15:57.630 --> 00:15:59.960
Now, as to my judgment...

00:16:00.730 --> 00:16:01.800
Yes?

00:16:02.360 --> 00:16:05.730
You'll be cast into space. You've just had your last meal.

00:16:05.830 --> 00:16:09.030
Ltjg. Cronicle Asher, you will carry out the sentence.

00:16:09.060 --> 00:16:11.660
Captain Tassilo, that's too harsh!

00:16:12.000 --> 00:16:14.660
Cronicle, don't anger me!

00:16:14.930 --> 00:16:17.600
Even if you are the queen's younger brother,

00:16:17.630 --> 00:16:19.930
your actions will demand a punishment of their own!

00:16:20.100 --> 00:16:23.830
Cronicle... I appreciate the thought.

00:16:24.200 --> 00:16:27.330
Captain, you've been very good to me.

00:16:27.360 --> 00:16:29.060
Thank you very much.

00:16:33.800 --> 00:16:36.600
Your advancement to full lieutenant is effective immediately.

00:16:36.630 --> 00:16:37.500
Sir.

00:16:37.900 --> 00:16:39.860
Be sure to carry out your instructions.

00:16:40.100 --> 00:16:41.000
Sir!

00:16:49.000 --> 00:16:50.360
That one looks fragile.

00:16:50.500 --> 00:16:51.460
What is it?

00:16:53.600 --> 00:16:55.760
Probably something off an old colony.

00:16:57.700 --> 00:16:58.630
I guess, but...

00:16:58.960 --> 00:16:59.830
You mean that?

00:16:59.860 --> 00:17:00.600
Yeah.

00:17:04.060 --> 00:17:05.400
A mobile suit?

00:17:05.430 --> 00:17:07.230
Do you also see the light in the window?

00:17:07.960 --> 00:17:09.260
Üso, no!

00:17:09.760 --> 00:17:11.330
Üso, where are you going?

00:17:11.360 --> 00:17:13.030
Don't go off on your own!

00:17:15.360 --> 00:17:18.360
There's a mobile suit there! Don't wander too close!

00:17:18.530 --> 00:17:20.460
An enemy would have fired on us by now.

00:17:23.030 --> 00:17:24.900
Just keep your rifle on it!

00:17:25.100 --> 00:17:26.060
I am.

00:17:29.400 --> 00:17:32.360
Üso! There's someone in the window. It's the enemy!

00:17:32.400 --> 00:17:33.560
Is it an enemy?

00:17:33.600 --> 00:17:35.900
You're the one who said it's a BESPA, Üso!

00:17:36.160 --> 00:17:38.760
But they wouldn't normally be in a place like this.

00:17:44.960 --> 00:17:46.900
It's definitely a BESPA mobile suit!

00:17:47.330 --> 00:17:48.260
Üso!

00:17:48.760 --> 00:17:51.330
If I don't come back, go back in the Gundam.

00:17:51.600 --> 00:17:54.000
Quit kidding around and get back here!

00:18:00.560 --> 00:18:01.630
Go away.

00:18:03.000 --> 00:18:05.260
You aren't adrift?

00:18:05.830 --> 00:18:08.460
Is there anything I can do to help?

00:18:08.500 --> 00:18:11.430
I don't need help! Get back to your shuttle!

00:18:22.630 --> 00:18:24.460
I told you to leave, didn't I?

00:18:25.460 --> 00:18:27.660
There's someone injured with you, isn't there?

00:18:27.700 --> 00:18:29.560
We don't need help from strangers!

00:18:29.830 --> 00:18:32.100
I especially won't ask for help...

00:18:32.130 --> 00:18:34.030
...from Earth Federation soldiers!

00:18:35.330 --> 00:18:36.900
I'm from the shuttle!

00:18:37.360 --> 00:18:38.660
I'm not a soldier!

00:18:38.900 --> 00:18:42.830
As if the absolutely neutral PCST would transport a Federation mobile suit?!

00:18:47.660 --> 00:18:51.960
As the law states, I've given you three days of oxygen and food.

00:18:52.060 --> 00:18:53.230
Thanks.

00:18:53.630 --> 00:18:57.830
It would have been funny for Lady Guillotine to go to the guillotine herself.

00:18:58.260 --> 00:18:59.560
It's better this way.

00:19:08.860 --> 00:19:11.160
Honor to Commander Fuala Griffon!

00:19:18.460 --> 00:19:21.300
Damn it!!!

00:19:39.130 --> 00:19:40.630
I think I'm going to vomit.

00:19:41.800 --> 00:19:44.530
This man's practically out of air!

00:19:44.800 --> 00:19:46.930
But you still won't ask for help?

00:19:47.300 --> 00:19:49.660
He's prepared to die an honorable death in battle.

00:19:49.900 --> 00:19:52.830
None of my men would ask a stranger for charity!

00:19:52.900 --> 00:19:53.860
Now leave!

00:19:53.960 --> 00:19:56.200
I'll take your mobile suit, too.

00:19:56.230 --> 00:19:57.260
Do what you like.

00:19:57.760 --> 00:20:00.000
Damn thing barely works.

00:20:04.460 --> 00:20:08.660
Stangam... Even though you fought so well...

00:20:09.230 --> 00:20:11.700
I... I was prepared for it...

00:20:12.200 --> 00:20:13.630
Should I give you some medicine?

00:20:14.230 --> 00:20:15.300
Yes...

00:20:15.760 --> 00:20:16.760
Like this?

00:20:16.900 --> 00:20:17.700
Okay.

00:20:19.500 --> 00:20:22.060
I'm against giving them even one canister of air!

00:20:22.400 --> 00:20:26.200
Unless engaged in battle, it's naval tradition to lend assistance.

00:20:26.500 --> 00:20:27.530
But...

00:20:36.030 --> 00:20:37.500
I know you can hear me.

00:20:37.730 --> 00:20:39.930
I'm putting the canisters here. I'm going now.

00:20:41.530 --> 00:20:43.830
Forcing kindness on others will get you killed.

00:20:44.530 --> 00:20:47.260
In Kasarelia... Where I come from,

00:20:47.300 --> 00:20:50.260
we always do this for travelers or people in need.

00:20:50.630 --> 00:20:53.000
Is something like this foolish?

00:20:57.930 --> 00:20:59.760
Damn right, it's foolish!

00:20:59.930 --> 00:21:02.630
And if I wanted, that bullet would have hit its mark!

00:21:05.260 --> 00:21:08.560
Kasarelia, huh? The place has a nice ring to it.

00:21:09.560 --> 00:21:10.660
Where is it?

00:21:10.700 --> 00:21:11.660
Earth.

00:21:12.000 --> 00:21:17.030
In a South Seas language, "kasarelia" means "Hello" or "So long."

00:21:17.230 --> 00:21:18.330
I see.

00:21:18.630 --> 00:21:20.430
I'm Lieutenant Godwald.

00:21:20.560 --> 00:21:21.700
Üso Ewin.

00:21:22.300 --> 00:21:24.130
Well, if you'll excuse me.

00:21:37.660 --> 00:21:38.800
Kasarelia!

00:21:40.930 --> 00:21:41.960
Kasarelia!

00:21:54.800 --> 00:21:58.460
Üso, there's a large object in the airspace ahead. Be careful!

00:21:59.800 --> 00:22:02.200
Don't shoot! That's a solar battery!

00:22:02.930 --> 00:22:03.930
Battery?

00:22:24.060 --> 00:22:29.530
Piercing the sky, Blue lightning
sora wo tsukisasu aoi inazuma

00:22:29.530 --> 00:22:35.320
Staining the earth, With the shadow of greed
daichi o someteku, yokubou no kage

00:22:36.370 --> 00:22:41.460
Once again, when the nightmare, Envelops the Earth
futatabi akumu ga, sekai wo tsutsumu toki

00:22:41.460 --> 00:22:46.790
You hear voices crying out "S.O.S."
"SOS" wo sakebu koe ga kikoeru...

00:22:48.630 --> 00:22:54.130
Let proud hope fill your heart
hokoritakaki kibou wo mune ni

00:22:54.720 --> 00:23:03.100
And stand up! Say a prayer for peace!!
tachiagare! heiwa no inori komete!

00:23:04.100 --> 00:23:05.100
WINNERS FOREVER!

00:23:06.100 --> 00:23:08.980
In every age
itsuno jidai mo

00:23:08.980 --> 00:23:14.570
...People take risks for freedom
hito wa jiyuu wo kakete

00:23:15.000 --> 00:23:17.000
WINNERS FOREVER!

00:23:18.330 --> 00:23:21.240
The battle goes on
tatakai tsuzukeru

00:23:21.240 --> 00:23:25.920
Fighting all alone in solitude
kodoku na made ni hitori...

00:23:33.030 --> 00:23:35.860
Going into space to search for his parents,

00:23:36.630 --> 00:23:41.360
Üso encounters children being held hostage by BESPA.

00:23:42.600 --> 00:23:48.800
Who would have imagined they'd end up stealing an enemy spaceship?

00:23:50.130 --> 00:23:53.360
Next time, on Mobile Suit Victory Gundam:

00:23:53.430 --> 00:23:55.930
Next Episode REINEFORCE, LIFTOFF
"Reineforce, Lift Off".

00:23:55.930 --> 00:23:55.960
Next Episode REINEFORCE, LIFTOFF

00:23:55.960 --> 00:23:57.430
Please watch it!

00:23:57.430 --> 00:23:59.400
Next Episode REINEFORCE, LIFTOFF
